TEXT -416 -288 Left 3 ;#412 Common-emitter amplifier - measuring the input impedance
TEXT -416 -232 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yhuf2_Zu8T8
TEXT -416 -184 Left 2 ;RSER is Alan's resistor substitution box. The series resistance that halves the base signal equals the amplifier's input impedance.
TEXT 944 -128 Left 2 !.step param Rseries list 1m 6.5k
TEXT 944 -80 Left 2 !.tran 0 20m 16m 1u
TEXT 944 -32 Left 2 !.meas tran CH1_PP PP V(base) FROM 16m TO 20m
TEXT 944 16 Left 2 !.meas tran CH2_PP PP V(collector) FROM 16m TO 20m
TEXT 944 64 Left 2 !.meas tran GAIN PARAM CH2_PP/CH1_PP
TEXT 944 144 Left 2 ;CH1_PP is what Alan reads on channel 1 while he turns the substitution box.
TEXT 944 192 Left 2 ;Base-to-collector gain is unchanged by RSER; only the signal reaching the base shrinks.
TEXT -416 432 Left 2 ;Alan starts with his substitution box at 0 and turns it up to 6.5k, where the base signal has halved. The
TEXT -416 480 Left 2 ;first step is 1 milliohm rather than 0 because LTspice rejects a zero-ohm resistor. RLOAD 1Meg stands in for the open output.
